      "spam": false,
      "value": "That would create complications of avatar interactions, especially those who are of a different scale.  Hand positions would not match, either on one viewer or both.  It would not match up.  Viewer of the player who sets the option would see someone who normally has a taller avatar reaching down and not where they are pointing OR the hands would be reaching up, and would not be placed properly.   If anything it should default to a generic, non-pose avatar.  \n\nIf you want a business meeting, you could either request all people participating to use a professional avatar or be removed.  No need for that option.  Honestly though, VRchat might not be the best place to have such a meeting.\n\nAnd while I do agree there are some avatars that... have gotten out of hand, it would be nice to block that avatar's ID so it won't be seen.  But as someone who values appearance and quite prideful of the work I have done, I would hate that people could just turn me off \"eww furry\"  but... then again, people like that probably aren't worth talking to.\n\nI guess I should say, I am on the fence with this idea... because I could see it's use for performance, especially in places where there's an event, and removing certain avatars... but at the same time, I'm more upset at players who purposefully use offensive avatars and creating a need for such a function to need creation...",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
