  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-17T04:35:48.911Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Allowing a user to select this and have all nearby players default to their PUBLIC model, would be cool (client side only of course). For younger users who dont wanna see all the... um, everything but still want to interact and chat. And Streamers who may want to have a clean stream for a moment while they AFK or something.\n- This could also be useful on a per player basis. Select a player and force their model to be defaulted. Sometimes you dont want to block someone (because you want to still talk to them), but their model is offensive. Could also help with performance issues if you make a high poly model default to a PUBLIC on with less verts.\n- Also useful for professional uses, like business meetings in VR, or virtual conventions. No need for models, just voice and presence.",
